Convert Array to Doubly Linked List — Quick Revision

Create the first array element as the head. Then traverse from index 1, create a new node for each element, and connect both directions using current.next = newNode and newNode.prev = current. Finally, return head.

Time: O(n)
Auxiliary Space: O(n) — n new linked-list nodes are created.

code
===================

/*
Definition for a Node.

class ListNode {
    public int data;
    public ListNode prev;
    public ListNode next;

    public ListNode();
    public ListNode(int data);
    public ListNode(int data, ListNode prev, ListNode next);
};
*/

class Solution {

    public ListNode arrayToDoublyLinkedList(List<Integer> arr) {

        // If the array/list is empty, return null
        if (arr.size() == 0) {
            return null;
        }

        // Create the first node
        // arr.get(0) gives the first element
        ListNode head = new ListNode(arr.get(0));

        // Current points to the last node created
        ListNode current = head;

        // Start from the second element
        for (int i = 1; i < arr.size(); i++) {

            // Create a new node using the current array element
            ListNode newNode = new ListNode(arr.get(i));

            // Connect current node to the new node
            current.next = newNode;

            // Connect new node back to the current node
            newNode.prev = current;

            // Move current to the newly created node
            current = newNode;
        }

        // Return the first node of the doubly linked list
        return head;
    }
}
